Feed Wayland touches into GPUI's TouchEvent.

What: gpui_linux's Wayland client binds `wl_touch` on a seat with the touch capability (once, as winit does; a seat
that loses it, or is replaced, cancels its touches) and turns `down`/`motion`/`up`/`cancel` into `TouchEvent`s:
`Started`/`Moved`/`Ended`, `Cancelled` for every touch still down on `cancel`, device `Touch`, surface-local
logical pixels (Wayland's surface coordinates are logical, so winit's physical-pixel scaling is dropped), an up at
the last motion's position. Wayland reuses `wl_touch` ids and GPUI never reuses a `TouchId`, so each down gets a
fresh one. `time_stamp` is the event's millisecond time moved onto GPUI's clock by its age against
`CLOCK_MONOTONIC` (what libinput-based compositors stamp with), as patch 0020 does on iOS and the web; an event
older than 10 s is on another base (a test client's made-up times) and is timed at dispatch. `frame`, `shape` and
`orientation` are ignored, as in winit: each event is delivered as it comes. A touch down's serial is recorded as a
press, so moves, popup grabs, selections and activation tokens work from a tap. Compositors never make pointer
events from `wl_touch`, so nothing is deduplicated.

New file `wayland/touch.rs`, ported from rust-windowing/winit src/platform_impl/linux/wayland/seat/touch/mod.rs @
v0.30.13 (45a6f047c7eb0d68f37138cbdd38eec9cd4c1575), Apache-2.0, Copyright the winit contributors (credited in
NOTICE); Flutter's Linux fl_touch_manager.cc @ 3.50.1 is the second reference. Its touch map and clock are pure,
with table tests (`touches_follow_wl_touch_events`, `touch_time_stamps`); `client.rs` holds only the dispatch glue.
A port, so one patch whatever its size (AGENTS.md patch rule 4).

Why: upstream's Wayland backend binds only `wl_pointer` and `wl_keyboard`, so a touchscreen on Wayland did nothing
in GPUI apps (compositors don't emulate a pointer for touch). The backend's seat handling is private, so neither a
Parallax crate nor an extension trait can add it. cfg: Linux/FreeBSD with the `wayland` feature, as the module is.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

